{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780244774,"nonce":"1CAOAyzR3qE1eNIq9VwnwqR6Wd4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABD7DJGg","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/48","origin":"github"},"title":"Temporal derivative fails when resampling fires on time-dep domain with multiple spatial tags","message":"## Bug\n\nWhen adaptive resampling fires on a time-dependent domain that has **multiple spatial tags with different point counts** (e.g. \\`domain.variable(\"interior\", sample=(N,None))\\` giving N=24 and \\`domain.variable(\"initial\")\\` giving N_initial ≠ N), training crashes with:\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nValueError: Temporal derivative expected scalar output per point, got shape (24,)\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe temporal derivative evaluator in \\`trace_evaluator.py\\` determines the number of collocation points \\`N\\` to vmap over. When the time variable is the global \\`\"__time__\"\\` (i.e. not a tag-specific time), \\`active_spatial_tag = None\\` and the fallback path uses:\n\n\\`\\`\\`python\nN = max(N, int(v.shape[point_axis(v)]))  # over ALL spatial tags in ctx\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nIn the resampling residual scoring context the evaluator receives **all** sampled spatial tags simultaneously — e.g. \\`\"interior\"` (N=24) and \\`\"initial\"\\` (N_initial=8). The fallback picks \\`N = max(24, 8) = 24\\`.\n\nThe \\`_local_context_for_point(idx)\\` helper then slices **only** tags whose size equals N=24. Because \\`\"interior\".shape[0] = 24 == N\\`, it gets sliced; but because \\`\"initial\".shape[0] = 8 ≠ N\\`, it is **not sliced** and remains as the full (8,1) array.\n\nWhen the PDE expression \\`u = net(t, x) * x*(1-x)\\` is evaluated with an unsliced \"initial\" context, the network accidentally receives **all 24 interior points** instead of the 1-point slice — producing shape \\`(24,)\\` rather than a scalar.\n\n## Minimal Reproducer\n\n\\`\\`\\`python\nimport jno, foundax, jax, optax\nfrom jno import sampler, LearningRateSchedule as lrs\n\nν = 0.05\ndomain = jno.domain(constructor=jno.domain.line(mesh_size=0.1), time=(0, 1.0, 4))\nx, t   = domain.variable(\"interior\", sample=(6, None), resampling_strategy=sampler.rad(resample_every=5, start_epoch=2))\nx0, t0 = domain.variable(\"initial\")\n\nnet = jno.nn.wrap(foundax.deeponet(n_sensors=1, coord_dim=1, n_outputs=1, n_layers=4, basis_functions=64, hidden_dim=48, key=jax.random.PRNGKey(3)))\nnet.optimizer(optax.adam(1), lr=lrs.warmup_cosine(10, 1, 1e-3, 1e-5))\nu = net(t, x) * x * (1 - x)\npde = jno.np.grad(u, t) + u * jno.np.grad(u, x) - ν * jno.np.grad(jno.np.grad(u, x), x)\nini = net(t0, x0) * x0 * (1 - x0) - jno.np.sin(jno.np.pi * x0)\njno.core([pde.mse, ini.mse], domain).solve(10)\n# → ValueError: Temporal derivative expected scalar output per point, got shape (6,)\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n## Expected Behaviour\n\nThe temporal derivative should correctly vmap over the \\`N\\` points that belong to the **expression being differentiated**, not the global maximum across all context tags. Training should complete without error.\n\n## Affected Code\n\n- \\`jno/trace_evaluator.py\\`: N determination fallback in the \\`Jacobian\\` temporal-derivative handler (~line 996–1012)\n\n## Impact\n\nThis bug prevents attaching residual-based resampling strategies (RAD, RARD, etc.) to time-dependent domains that also sample an initial-condition or boundary tag. The only workaround before this fix was to reformulate as a 2D spatial (rect) domain — losing the time-windowed training benefits.","files":null}]}